@page "/"

<PageTitle>Tools — Evaluated Applications</PageTitle>

<header class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
        <span class="eyebrow">Interactive tools · running in your browser</span>
        <h1>Touch the tech.</h1>
        <p class="lede">These tools run our .NET libraries client-side, compiled to WebAssembly. No server, no upload —
            the work happens on your machine and nothing leaves the tab.</p>
    </div>
</header>

<section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="grid">
            <a class="card tool" href="/tools/analyst" style="--cat:var(--c-holodb, #66c1aa)">
                <div class="card-top"><h3>The Analyst</h3><span class="tag live">live</span><span class="ver">HoloDb</span></div>
                <p class="desc">Paste any data and profile it with a real SQL database in your browser — types,
                    distributions, anomalies, hidden entities — then query it at a live SQL prompt.</p>
                <div class="go-in">Open The Analyst →</div>
            </a>
            <a class="card tool" href="/tools/creature" style="--cat:linear-gradient(90deg, var(--c-algformer, #5998ff) 0%, var(--c-algformer, #5998ff) 50%, var(--c-tracer, #f0796a) 50%, var(--c-tracer, #f0796a) 100%); --cat-root:var(--c-algformer, #5998ff)">
                <div class="card-top"><h3>The Creature</h3><span class="tag live">live</span><span class="ver">AlgFormer · Tracer</span></div>
                <p class="desc">Raise a creature that learns to navigate a world you draw — a holographic transformer
                    for its brain, our pathfinder for its feet.</p>
                <div class="go-in">Open The Creature →</div>
            </a>
            <a class="card tool" href="/tools/forecaster" style="--cat:var(--c-algformer, #5998ff)">
                <div class="card-top"><h3>The Forecaster</h3><span class="tag live">live</span><span class="ver">AlgFormer</span></div>
                <p class="desc">Train the same holographic transformer on real historical price ticks — click to
                    train it live, and watch its next-move accuracy climb as it learns the tape.</p>
                <div class="go-in">Open The Forecaster →</div>
            </a>
            <a class="card tool" href="/tools/prism" style="--cat:var(--c-algformer, #5998ff)">
                <div class="card-top"><h3>Prism</h3><span class="tag live">live</span><span class="ver">AlgFormer</span></div>
                <p class="desc">Say something to a tiny AI that runs entirely in your browser — a real, trained
                    model, computed live on your own device. It's still learning, so expect rough replies.</p>
                <div class="go-in">Open Prism →</div>
            </a>
            <a class="card tool" href="/tools/stories" style="--cat:var(--c-algformer, #5998ff)">
                <div class="card-top"><h3>Nano Stories</h3><span class="tag live">live</span><span class="ver">AlgFormer</span></div>
                <p class="desc">The exact same model as Prism — same weights, same training run — asked to write
                    a story instead of hold a conversation. Give it an opening line and watch it continue live.</p>
                <div class="go-in">Open Nano Stories →</div>
            </a>
            <a class="card tool" href="/tools/prose" style="--cat:linear-gradient(90deg, var(--c-holodb, #66c1aa) 0%, var(--c-holodb, #66c1aa) 50%, var(--c-algformer, #5998ff) 50%, var(--c-algformer, #5998ff) 100%); --cat-root:var(--c-holodb, #66c1aa)">
                <div class="card-top"><h3>Prose</h3><span class="tag live">live</span><span class="ver">HoloDb · AlgFormer</span></div>
                <p class="desc">Paste in a body of text and a real English grammar mines it, in your browser, then
                    recombines what it learned into sentences and Q&amp;A pairs you can copy straight into a
                    training corpus.</p>
                <div class="go-in">Open Prose →</div>
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
